    "description": "What: the bt-window-duel cast on bt-range (CE-5033, glass windows GW-2; docs/DESIGN_Glass_Windows.md §7): 'Window Rifleman' (Friend, upstairs in House A at (107.1,100.9), z 3) defends the house from beside its upstairs south window (glazed, x 106.5..107.7 on y 100) and 'Street Rifleman' (Hostile, in the open at (108.5,80) behind 'Van 1') attacks him. Standard behaviours only; nothing scripted. Judge: the window's pane is whole before anyone fires; the Window Rifleman's FIRST shot out through it breaks it at once (his muzzle is within 1.5 m of the pane — a man firing out, D-4), within a second of the shot; and the Street Rifleman still sees and fires at him (glass changes no visibility)."
